{"id":"peers-per-pupil","title":"Spending and revenue per pupil against ten like districts","question":"Kind of spending by kind of spending, where does San Francisco sit among large California districts, and where is it furthest from the middle?","finding":"In fiscal 2024 San Francisco spent $25,249 per pupil day to day, rank 3 of 11 (the middle of the ten peers: $23,161). Furthest above the peer middle: general administration $400 against $244 (+64%); pupil transport $763 against $468 (+63%); pupil support services $2,573 against $1,656 (+55%); other support services $231 against $150 (+54%). Furthest below: running and upkeep of buildings $1,639 against $2,248 (-27%). Its money comes from a different place: $17,492 per pupil from local sources against $7,978 at the middle peer, and rank 9 of 11 for State money.","how":"Each line of the federal school-finance survey divided by the district's own October pupil count, fiscal 2019 to 2024, for San Francisco (district and county office together) and Elk Grove Unified, Fresno Unified, Long Beach Unified, Los Angeles Unified, Oakland Unified, Sacramento City Unified, San Bernardino City Unified, San Diego Unified, San Jose Unified, Santa Ana Unified. Rank 1 is the highest of the eleven. The middle is the median of the ten peers. Years before fiscal 2019 are left out because pupil counts then included charter pupils whose schools' spending is not in the survey, to a different degree in each district.","limits":"The ten peers were chosen for this project as large city districts; they are not matched on pupil need, school size or wages, and their county offices of education are separate bodies whose services to them are not in their figures, which can make San Francisco look dearer. Districts code the same cost to different categories. Local money in San Francisco includes parcel taxes and the City contributions shown on the City-money screen. A district where living costs are high must pay more to hire and keep staff, and one with many small schools, or with many pupils who are learning English, have disabilities or are poor, will spend more per pupil for honest reasons; none of those is measured here.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"measure","t":"Per pupil","type":"text"},{"k":"sf","t":"San Francisco, fiscal 2024","type":"usd"},{"k":"peerMedian","t":"Middle of ten peers","type":"usd"},{"k":"gap","t":"Above or below the middle","type":"pct"},{"k":"rank","t":"Rank of 11 (1 = highest)","type":"int"},{"k":"ranks","t":"Rank each year","type":"text"},{"k":"highest","t":"Highest","type":"text"},{"k":"lowest","t":"Lowest","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"measure":"General administration","sf":400,"peerMedian":244,"gap":0.64,"rank":2,"highest":"Los Angeles Unified $749","lowest":"Long Beach Unified $111","ranks":"2018-19: 1, 2019-20: 2, 2020-21: 1, 2021-22: 2, 2022-23: 1, 2023-24: 2"},{"measure":"Pupil transport","sf":763,"peerMedian":468,"gap":0.632,"rank":2,"highest":"San Bernardino City Unified $770","lowest":"Long Beach Unified $272","ranks":"2018-19: 1, 2019-20: 1, 2020-21: 9, 2021-22: 1, 2022-23: 1, 2023-24: 2"},{"measure":"Pupil support services","sf":2573,"peerMedian":1656,"gap":0.554,"rank":1,"highest":"San Francisco (district and county office) $2,573","lowest":"Oakland Unified $986","ranks":"2018-19: 1, 2019-20: 1, 2020-21: 1, 2021-22: 2, 2022-23: 1, 2023-24: 1"},{"measure":"Other support services","sf":231,"peerMedian":150,"gap":0.538,"rank":1,"highest":"San Francisco (district and county office) $231","lowest":"Elk Grove Unified $124","ranks":"2018-19: 1, 2019-20: 1, 2020-21: 2, 2021-22: 2, 2022-23: 2, 2023-24: 1"},{"measure":"Business, central and other support services","sf":1278,"peerMedian":864,"gap":0.479,"rank":1,"highest":"San Francisco (district and county office) $1,278","lowest":"Elk Grove Unified $707","ranks":"2018-19: 2, 2019-20: 2, 2020-21: 2, 2021-22: 1, 2022-23: 1, 2023-24: 1"},{"measure":"Running and upkeep of buildings","sf":1639,"peerMedian":2248,"gap":-0.271,"ra